// shader-differential — discard on the FALSE arm of a branch (t_79fc6bf7).
//
// The kill is reached through `else`, so the fragment that survives is
// the one that satisfied the branch condition.  Under the rig's VP,
// TEXCOORD0.w runs 0.912 -> -0.072 left to right, so `a > 0.5` holds on
// the 27 left-hand columns: the reference paints those 1728 pixels and
// kills the other 2368.  A lowering that recovers the guard from the
// LAST COMPARISON SEEN instead of the PATH CONDITION emits the same
// SGTRC but predicates the KIL on NE rather than EQ, and kills exactly
// the fragments that must survive: every pixel differs.  Measured by
// claude against the reference, 2026-09-02 08:58 (the default path,
// shipping; the general path refuses the shape until CF-2 lands).
//
// Curated on the default path, RED until t_79fc6bf7 is fixed.  Whatever
// lands for it must turn this row identical with painted a = b = 1728.
void main(float4 color : TEXCOORD0, out float4 oColor : COLOR)
{
    float4 c = color;
    if (c.a > 0.5f) {
        oColor = c;
    } else {
        discard;
    }
}
